  "light": {
    "$comment": "Light-appearance brand colors per palette. Every palette, preset or custom, applies in both appearances: dark uses `palettes`, light uses these brand colors on the existing white light surfaces. `ink` = text/icons/strokes on the light page; `textSafe` = body-size text; `fill*` / `grad*` = filled shapes that carry `onPrimary` text; `soft` = tinted chip background; `bgTop` / `bgBottom` = page background gradient; `pill` = model pill background; `accent` = second brand color (name gradient end, glows). The default palette keeps the hand-tuned light values below; every other entry is generated by the light-brand derivation that each client reproduces from `lightBrand` cases. Tabs: the default palette keeps per-tab light colors, other palettes use `ink` for all tabs.",
    "derivation": {
      "$steps": [
        "1. H = OKLCH hue of the dark palette primary; AH = hue of its accent.",
        "2. Each key starts at fromOklch(ladder[key].L, ladder[key].C, H) (accent uses AH). The ladder is measured from the hand-tuned default light purple.",
        "3. Darken by `step` (not below minLightness) until: ink ≥ minInkText and accent ≥ minInk on bgTop; textSafe ≥ minText on white, bgTop and soft.",
        "4. Fill mode: bright when the OKLCH chroma of fromOklch(bright.gradStart, ladder.gradStart.C, H) is higher than at ladder.gradStart.L. Bright: onPrimary = the dark palette onPrimary; fill / fillText / fillPressed / gradStart / gradEnd start at `bright` lightness and are lightened by `step` (≤ maxLightness) until onPrimary ≥ minText. White: onPrimary = #FFFFFF; fill = ink, fillText = textSafe; fillPressed / gradStart / gradEnd darken until white ≥ minText.",
        "5. Contrast rules (checkLight): ink ≥ minInkText and accent ≥ minInk on bgTop; textSafe ≥ minText on white / bgTop / soft; onPrimary ≥ minInk on fill (icon-only fills) and ≥ minText on fillText / fillPressed / gradStart / gradEnd."
      ],
